# Copy to .npmrc (or merge into your existing .npmrc) when consuming
# `@makenotion/lore` as a devDependency on npm or Yarn 1.
# Yarn Berry / Yarn 4 consumers configure this in `.yarnrc.yml` instead
# (see the "Using @makenotion/lore as a devDep" section in lore's
# README).
#
# 1. Map the @makenotion scope to GitHub Packages so `npm install` /
#    `yarn add -D @makenotion/lore` resolves there instead of the public
#    npm registry.
@makenotion:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com

# 2. Authenticate to GitHub Packages. The package's visibility is
#    INTERNAL inside the makenotion GitHub org — members can read it,
#    no public access.
#
#    Easiest path (no PAT to manage):
#
#      gh auth refresh -h github.com -s read:packages
#      export GITHUB_PACKAGES_TOKEN="$(gh auth token)"
#
#    Fallback path (Personal Access Token):
#
#      Create a Classic PAT with `read:packages` scope at
#      https://github.com/settings/tokens/new, OR a fine-grained PAT
#      scoped to Repository -> Packages: Read-only at
#      https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new, then
#      `export GITHUB_PACKAGES_TOKEN=<token>` in your shell rc.
#
#    Do NOT commit a populated .npmrc.
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${GITHUB_PACKAGES_TOKEN}
